        "created_at": "2017-08-10T17:08:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>\n[quote=\"Eric R\"]\n</p><p>all the Spirits are gender-neutral - or more accurately, gender-NA. \"His\" should be \"its\", or optionally \"their\".</p><p>\n[/quote]\n</p><p>Does this imply that the Dahan language has no distinction in gender in its pronouns (sort of like Chinese, at least verbally) or do they have a gender neutral pronoun (like Russian)? &nbsp;</p><p>If the latter, when Thunderspeaker takes human form, do the Dahan refer to them with the pronoun that they manifested as, or as gender neutral?</p>",
